!! Example

```javascript
// Traditional exponential backoff
var delay = 100;
setTimeout(retry1, delay);
delay *= 2;
setTimeout(retry2, delay);
delay *= 2;
setTimeout(retry3, delay);

// Wave scheduler
var scheduler = $tw.utils.WaveScheduler.createExponentialBackoff(100, 2, 30000);
setTimeout(retry1, scheduler.next()); // 200ms
setTimeout(retry2, scheduler.next()); // 400ms
setTimeout(retry3, scheduler.next()); // 800ms
```

The Wave Scheduler realizes the vision of programming as specifying laws of motion rather than enumerating steps, making it a fundamental new primitive alongside functions and types.
